# Access-tier annotations for the US FSMA 204 extension (ESPR Article 9 tiers).
# One entry per term; merged into the module by scripts/build-json.ts.
#
# FSMA 204 (FDA Food Traceability Rule, 21 CFR Part 1 Subpart S) is a US regime;
# the ESPR tier vocabulary is reused only to express default field visibility.
# Traceability RECORDS under the rule are made available to FDA on request
# (21 CFR 1.1455(b)), but this module's single term is not record content: it
# declares which category of the FDA's published Food Traceability List the
# trade item falls under, and that list membership is public information.
# Tier re-reviewed 2026-07 and kept Public; not locked (no EU act applies), so
# deployments may tighten at runtime. Terms not listed default to
# AuthorizedOnly.

@prefix usfsma: <https://ref.openepcis.io/extensions/us/fsma204/> .
@prefix oec:    <https://ref.openepcis.io/extensions/common/core/> .


# --- Public: Food Traceability List category classification ---

usfsma:hasFoodTraceabilityListCategory oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:Public ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "The FTL category only restates that the product falls under a category of the FDA's publicly published Food Traceability List, revealing scope of the rule rather than any traceability record content (which goes to FDA on request per 21 CFR 1.1455(b))." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://www.fda.gov/food/food-safety-modernization-act-fsma/food-traceability-list> .
